\begin{abstract}
  \noindent
  For the TCS Summer Event we run a gamified agentic-AI workshop where
  teams of academics build a small game with Claude Code.  We want
  maximum parallel participation: participants use their own laptops
  and SSH into the facilitator's laptop, which runs the Docker
  container described here.  Every connection spawns a fresh
  [[claude]] session, but everyone on the same team always lands in
  the same working directory, so a team continues one shared project
  across connections and teammates.  Project files and Claude's
  session transcripts persist on the host for post-event evaluation.
\end{abstract}
